{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_populate_populate_py", "label": "populate.py \u2014 an element on every axis of every index", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/POPULATE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Give it a ground-state atomic number and it returns that element and every ion of it on every coordinate the books define."}, {"id": "docs_populate_two_halves", "label": "Both halves of the method equation", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/POPULATE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Register 1206: R places the cells and the channel equation values them, meeting for the first time on this index."}, {"id": "docs_populate_status_vocabulary", "label": "READ, PINNED, DERIVED, RECOVERED, RECONSTRUCTED", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/POPULATE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "It never prints a value without its status; a RECOVERED defect and a READ one are different objects and the report never merges them."}, {"id": "docs_populate_outside_caps", "label": "It never silently places an element outside the caps", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/POPULATE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The report says OUTSIDE and names the cap that fails; a cell can satisfy all seven of section 7.1's constraints and still not be a cell of Lambda-8 at these caps."}, {"id": "docs_populate_never_repairs", "label": "When a reconstruction disagrees with the record, the finding is about the reconstruction", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/POPULATE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "G0c: where the recomputed value differs from the recorded one the report carries both."}, {"id": "docs_populate_collapse_ramp", "label": "C(Z, l) recovered as a linear ramp eight wide", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/POPULATE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "No member states its form, so it was inverted out of COORDINATES-2.13's computed column and comes back exact, reaching 0.5 at the Janet boundary. The first implementation was an indicator and the index rejected it."}, {"id": "docs_populate_b_column_withdrawn_table", "label": "The B column was built on a withdrawn configuration table", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/POPULATE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Aufbau reproduces 98.72% against observed 97.66%, and every disagreement lands on the elements where the two tables part company \u2014 Pd and Lr being the two register 1306 names when it withdraws aufbau. COORDINATES-2.13 was never rebuilt and nothing dockets it."}, {"id": "docs_populate_b_column_overloaded", "label": "The B column is overloaded", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/POPULATE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "104,807 rows carry the integer Pauli bound and 25 measured rows carry a float dispersion, so csv_bound returns None there rather than comparing an integer against a spread."}, {"id": "docs_populate_ladder_mapping", "label": "An element is not a cell", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/POPULATE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A Lambda-8 cell is a transition, so a mapping had to be chosen; the ionisation ladder is one mapping and not the mapping, and nothing in the store fixes it, so it stays RECONSTRUCTED."}], "edge